id: pm-o360q6
title: Agent-task transcript recovery accepts a refusal as a successful retry
description: "CodeRabbit review on PR #1133 found that a step with recovery_for may itself declare expected_output_kind=refusal. The parser verifies only that the referenced prior step is a refusal, allowing a failed retry to satisfy the recovery topology. Require recovery steps to be non-refusal successful outcomes and add adversarial parser coverage."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:sdk",contracts,recovery,review-feedback
created_at: "2026-08-27T19:11:48.651Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T12:52:27.789Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T12:52:27.068Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T12:52:27.068Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: recovery_for still references an earlier refusal; the recovery step cannot declare refusal output; adversarial parser coverage proves failed retries are rejected; exact coverage and static gates pass
parent: pm-8pnj
resolution: The SDK transcript parser requires every recovery_for step to use a successful output family; its defining parser module is canonically linked and terminal field-value assertions are parsed and validated.
expected_result: Recovery topology rejects refusal-as-retry and canonical PM evidence identifies the defining parser source.
actual_result: "The parser rejects refusal recovery, malformed and non-finite field-value assertions, and the focused 20-test SDK output-contract suite passes with the parser module linked."
